## 5. What The Walkthrough Explains

The human walkthrough accurately explains the audited Real Local DRS Resolver /
Writeback v0.1 runtime layer. It shows that Hedgehog OS can now locally write
semantic memory, resolve candidate memory, and record RootFinal-derived
outcomes while preserving Root authority.

Core explanation:

* DRS records do not become truth.
* DRS hits do not become authority.
* Reuse candidates do not become permission.
* Writeback does not become action.
* Root remains final authority.

